MatePad: keep a window's content when its buffer scale changes.

A Qt Widgets popup (e.g. Plasma's desktop context menu) on a 1x screen next to
a 2x screen was first given a 2x buffer and then, on wl_surface.enter, a 1x
one. QWaylandWindow::handleScreensChanged() changes mScale and calls
ensureSize(); the shm backing store then needs a buffer of a new size, which
starts empty (transparent), and nothing repaints the whole window: the
widget repaint manager only paints what becomes dirty, and the screen-change
event repaints only when the QScreen changes. Rows of the menu stayed
transparent until the pointer passed over them. Fill the new buffer with the
old content, scaled, so the window is complete; later paints refine it.

--- a/src/client/qwaylandshmbackingstore.cpp
+++ b/src/client/qwaylandshmbackingstore.cpp
@@ -276,6 +276,15 @@ void QWaylandShmBackingStore::resize(const QSize &size)
     qreal scale = waylandWindow()->scale();
     QSize sizeWithMargins = (size + QSize(margins.left()+margins.right(),margins.top()+margins.bottom())) * scale;
 
+    // On a buffer scale change the new buffer has a different size and would
+    // start empty, while only dirty regions get repainted: keep the old
+    // content, scaled (getBuffer() may delete the old buffer, so copy first).
+    QImage oldContent;
+    if (mBackBuffer && mBackBuffer->image()->devicePixelRatio() != scale
+        && mBackBuffer->size() != sizeWithMargins) {
+        oldContent = mBackBuffer->image()->copy();
+    }
+
     // We look for a free buffer to draw into. If the buffer is not the last buffer we used,
     // that is mBackBuffer, and the size is the same we memcpy the old content into the new
     // buffer so that QPainter is happy to find the stuff it had drawn before. If the new
@@ -297,6 +306,14 @@ void QWaylandShmBackingStore::resize(const QSize &size)
     if (mBackBuffer != buffer && oldSizeInBytes == newSizeInBytes)
         memcpy(buffer->image()->bits(), mBackBuffer->image()->constBits(), newSizeInBytes);
 
+    if (!oldContent.isNull()) {
+        QPainter p(buffer->image());
+        p.setCompositionMode(QPainter::CompositionMode_Source);
+        p.setRenderHint(QPainter::SmoothPixmapTransform);
+        p.drawImage(QRectF(QPointF(0, 0), QSizeF(buffer->image()->size()) / scale), oldContent,
+                    QRectF(oldContent.rect()));
+    }
+
     mBackBuffer = buffer;
 
     // ensure the new buffer is at the beginning of the list so next time getBuffer() will pick
